# only READ may be shared by any thread, and one that is only WRITTEN is a
# single-threaded mutable static; both at once is a data race (Rust's
# `static mut`). Here the spawned closure reads `counter` and `bump` assigns it:
# the write site is rejected, naming where the other thread reads it.
# thread_local(counter) is the per-thread spelling; an AtomicI32 the shared one.
